{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-35830" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the horizontal asymptote of the function $f(x)=\\frac{9{x}^{5}+3{x}^{2}+11}{12{x}^{5}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038578/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb18f17c790379288bafc4199eff65321ddd08317e927e19909d729df23627fd"} {"question" "q-35830" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The horizontal asymptote is $y={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{5}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{9{x}^{5}+3{x}^{2}+11}{12{x}^{5}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{9{x}^{5}}{{x}^{5}}+\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{{x}^{5}}+\\frac{11}{{x}^{5}})}{(\\frac{12{x}^{5}}{{x}^{5}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(9+\\frac{3}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{11}{{x}^{5}})}{(12)} \\\\  & =\\frac{9+0+0}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, the horizontal asymptote of $f(x)$ is $y=\\frac{3}{4}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038578/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb18f17c790379288bafc4199eff65321ddd08317e927e19909d729df23627fd"} {"question" "q-35830" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038578/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b0536130743b41b6ce862829ee1e55c1ddca652ab6528f6a3c939f10cb01d69c"} {"question" "q-35830" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038578/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb18f17c790379288bafc4199eff65321ddd08317e927e19909d729df23627fd"} {"question" "q-35830" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=0"] ["math" "y=\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{3}{4}"] ["text" "No horizontal asymptote"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038578/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb18f17c790379288bafc4199eff65321ddd08317e927e19909d729df23627fd"} {"question" "q-35830" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{3}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038578/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb18f17c790379288bafc4199eff65321ddd08317e927e19909d729df23627fd"} {"question" "q-35833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the horizontal asymptote of the function $f(x)=\\frac{4{x}^{2}-9x+1}{x+4}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038578/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb18f17c790379288bafc4199eff65321ddd08317e927e19909d729df23627fd"} {"question" "q-35833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The horizontal asymptote is $y={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is $x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{4{x}^{2}-9x+1}{x+4} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{4{x}^{2}}{x}-\\frac{9x}{x}+\\frac{1}{x})}{(\\frac{x}{x}+\\frac{4}{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(4x-9+\\frac{1}{x})}{(1+\\frac{4}{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(4x-9+0)}{(1+0)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(4x)-9 \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe limit does not come out to a finite number. Therefore, there is no horizontal asymptote." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038578/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb18f17c790379288bafc4199eff65321ddd08317e927e19909d729df23627fd"} {"question" "q-35833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038578/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b0536130743b41b6ce862829ee1e55c1ddca652ab6528f6a3c939f10cb01d69c"} {"question" "q-35833" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038578/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb18f17c790379288bafc4199eff65321ddd08317e927e19909d729df23627fd"} {"question" "q-35833" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-9"] ["math" "y=0"] ["math" "y=1"] ["math" "y=4"] ["text" "No horizontal asymptote"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038578/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb18f17c790379288bafc4199eff65321ddd08317e927e19909d729df23627fd"} {"question" "q-35833" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "No horizontal asymptote"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038578/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb18f17c790379288bafc4199eff65321ddd08317e927e19909d729df23627fd"} {"question" "q-68048" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{4{x}^{5}-9}{{x}^{3}+8x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038578/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb18f17c790379288bafc4199eff65321ddd08317e927e19909d729df23627fd"} {"question" "q-68048" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{3}.$ Then, by noting that the reciprocals shrink to $0$ in the limit, we can then evaluate the resulting expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{4{x}^{5}-9}{{x}^{3}+8x} & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{(\\frac{4{x}^{5}}{{x}^{3}}-\\frac{9}{{x}^{3}})}{(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{8x}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{(4{x}^{2}-\\frac{9}{{x}^{3}})}{(1+\\frac{8}{{x}^{2}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{4{x}^{2}-0}{1+0} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }4{x}^{2} \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038578/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb18f17c790379288bafc4199eff65321ddd08317e927e19909d729df23627fd"} {"question" "q-68048" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038578/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b0536130743b41b6ce862829ee1e55c1ddca652ab6528f6a3c939f10cb01d69c"} {"question" "q-68048" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038578/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb18f17c790379288bafc4199eff65321ddd08317e927e19909d729df23627fd"} {"question" "q-68048" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\infty "] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1/4"] ["math" "\\infty "] ["text" "Does not exist."]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038578/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb18f17c790379288bafc4199eff65321ddd08317e927e19909d729df23627fd"} {"question" "q-68048" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\infty "] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038578/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb18f17c790379288bafc4199eff65321ddd08317e927e19909d729df23627fd"} {"question" "q-68075" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the horizontal asymptote of $y=f(x)$ where $f(x)=\\frac{5+7{x}^{3}}{12x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038578/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb18f17c790379288bafc4199eff65321ddd08317e927e19909d729df23627fd"} {"question" "q-68075" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The horizontal asymptote is $y={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is $x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{5+7{x}^{3}}{12x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{5}{x}+\\frac{7{x}^{3}}{x})}{(\\frac{12x}{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{5}{x}+7{x}^{2})}{12} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(0+7{x}^{2})}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{12}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{x}^{2} \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe limit does not come out to a finite number. Therefore, there is no horizontal asymptote." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038578/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb18f17c790379288bafc4199eff65321ddd08317e927e19909d729df23627fd"} {"question" "q-68075" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038578/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b0536130743b41b6ce862829ee1e55c1ddca652ab6528f6a3c939f10cb01d69c"} {"question" "q-68075" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038578/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb18f17c790379288bafc4199eff65321ddd08317e927e19909d729df23627fd"} {"question" "q-68075" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-\\frac{7}{12}"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{12}"] ["text" "No horizontal asymptote"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038578/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb18f17c790379288bafc4199eff65321ddd08317e927e19909d729df23627fd"} {"question" "q-68075" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "No horizontal asymptote"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038578/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb18f17c790379288bafc4199eff65321ddd08317e927e19909d729df23627fd"} {"question" "q-106697" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{{x}^{7}-3{x}^{2}+4x}{{x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}+5}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038578/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb18f17c790379288bafc4199eff65321ddd08317e927e19909d729df23627fd"} {"question" "q-106697" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{4}.$ Then, by noting that the reciprocals shrink to $0$ in the limit, we can then evaluate the resulting expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{{x}^{7}-3{x}^{2}+4x}{{x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}+5} & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{(\\frac{{x}^{7}}{{x}^{4}}-\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{{x}^{4}}+\\frac{4x}{{x}^{4}})}{(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{{x}^{4}}-\\frac{3{x}^{3}}{{x}^{4}}+\\frac{5}{{x}^{4}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{({x}^{3}-\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{4}{{x}^{3}})}{(1-\\frac{3}{x}+\\frac{5}{{x}^{4}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\,\\,\\frac{({x}^{3}-0+0)}{(1-0+0)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\,\\,{x}^{3} \\\\  & =-\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038578/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb18f17c790379288bafc4199eff65321ddd08317e927e19909d729df23627fd"} {"question" "q-106697" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038578/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b0536130743b41b6ce862829ee1e55c1ddca652ab6528f6a3c939f10cb01d69c"} {"question" "q-106697" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038578/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb18f17c790379288bafc4199eff65321ddd08317e927e19909d729df23627fd"} {"question" "q-106697" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-\\infty "] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\infty "] ["math" "\\text{DNE}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038578/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb18f17c790379288bafc4199eff65321ddd08317e927e19909d729df23627fd"} {"question" "q-106697" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\infty "] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038578/state.json" "file_sha256" "fb18f17c790379288bafc4199eff65321ddd08317e927e19909d72